# Full HMMWV: free-flying sprung mass on four independent double-wishbone
# corners, each on its own shaker post, plus a rack-and-pinion steering rack
# feeding the two front tie rods. This is the whole vehicle -- the quartercar
# (front corner) and halfcar (rear axle) test rigs assembled into one body,
# with the front tierods rerouted from the chassis onto a steerable rack so
# the front wheels actually turn. Hardpoints, masses, and inertias are the
# HMMWV data shipped with Project Chrono (data/vehicle/hmmwv/): suspensions
# HMMWV_DoubleWishboneFront/Rear.json, chassis HMMWV_Chassis.json (2086.52 kg),
# steering HMMWV_RackPinion.json, wheel 18.8 kg + tire 37.6 kg per corner,
# tire radius 0.467. Axle stations and the steering rack come from
# HMMWV_Vehicle.json (wheelbase 3.378, suspension locations +-1.688965).
#
# Axes are ISO vehicle: x forward, y outboard-left, z up. The BASE FRAME sits
# on the VEHICLE CENTERLINE (y=0), at DESIGN WHEEL-CENTER HEIGHT (z=0), at
# MID-WHEELBASE (x=0, midway between the axles). A Chrono suspension-subsystem
# hardpoint maps to this frame by adding the axle's suspension location
# (+-1.688965, 0, 0) and the wheel-center height shift (0, 0, +0.026) that
# lifts the spindle COM (z=-0.026) onto z=0. Left-side hardpoints are used as
# given; the right side is the mirror image (negate y), exactly how Chrono
# mirrors one side's JSON to build the other. Front corners use the FRONT
# suspension JSON, rear corners the REAR JSON -- same wheel/tire/arm parts,
# only the axle-specific hardpoints, uprights, and spring/shock curves differ.
# Every loop closes at the design pose (all q = 0, chassis and spindles at
# identity quaternion).
#
# Topology (18 bodies, tree nv 43, nc 32, mobility 11):
#   0  chassis   floating   the whole sprung mass, free-flying (RBDA sec 9.4):
#                           full HMMWV chassis mass 2086.52 kg and centroidal
#                           inertia, quaternion attitude so no gimbal lock in
#                           any ride/handling attitude. All eight control arms
#                           and the steering rack hang off this body. Unlike
#                           quartercar (chassis on a vertical slider) and
#                           halfcar (chassis on a heave+roll chain), here the
#                           sprung mass has all six rigid-body DOF -- heave,
#                           roll, pitch, yaw, and lateral/longitudinal drift.
#   1  rack      prismatic y the steering rack (HMMWV_RackPinion steering link),
#                           sliding laterally on the chassis: a POSITION
#                           DRIVER. Drive its q through its own tau slot (a
#                           stiff PD servo tracking the commanded rack travel,
#                           i.e. the pinion angle times 0.1 m radius). Moving
#                           the rack pushes/pulls both front tie rods and so
#                           steers the front wheels about their kingpin axes.
#
#   Front-left corner (bodies 2..5), mirror front-right (6..9), then
#   rear-left (10..13) and rear-right (14..17). Each corner is one quartercar
#   (front) or halfcar-side (rear):
#     LCA      revolute x   lower wishbone; Chrono's pivot axis is exactly x
#                           (front/back chassis pivots share y,z), frame at
#                           their midpoint
#     UCA      revolute x   upper wishbone; the real pivot axis is skewed a
#                           few deg from x, idealized to x (as in quartercar/
#                           halfcar) since tree joints are axis-aligned; frame
#                           at the front/back midpoint
#     spindle  floating     upright + spindle + wheel + tire lumped (no
#                           wheel-spin DOF), located by the loop joints; frame
#                           at the wheel center. Parented to the base, not the
#                           chassis -- it is a floating body pinned entirely by
#                           constraints, exactly as in quartercar/halfcar
#                           (spherical tree joints aren't implemented).
#     post     prismatic z  shaker pad at the contact patch: a POSITION DRIVER,
#                           one per corner. Drive its q through its own tau slot.
#
# Loop joints, 4 per corner x 4 = 16 (each spindle carries ball joints
# everywhere, so like quartercar it is a floating body held by constraints):
#   spherical  LCA outer ball  -> spindle lower ball
#   spherical  UCA outer ball  -> spindle upper ball
#   distance   tie rod -> spindle steering-arm point.  FRONT: predecessor is
#              the RACK, so rack travel steers the wheel (this is the steering
#              geometry).  REAR: predecessor is the CHASSIS (Chrono's rear
#              tierod is grounded on the chassis at both ends -- the rear
#              doesn't steer), an ordinary fixed link. Either way it kills the
#              leftover spin about the kingpin axis.
#   distance   driver rod, post pad -> wheel center, length = tire radius: a
#              rigid "tire" with balls at patch and hub, exactly as in
#              quartercar/halfcar. Pins spindle height to post height; lateral
#              scrub during travel just tilts it (height error ~ s^2/2r).
#
# Mobility 11 = chassis (6, free-flying) + steering rack (1) + four posts (4).
# Each corner's LCA+UCA+spindle (8 tree DOF) is exactly balanced by its 8 loop
# constraints, so a corner adds no independent DOF: suspension deflection is
# the chassis-vs-post motion through the linkage, and steer is the rack. Tire
# loads (and any longitudinal/lateral force, which the vertical posts and
# tire rods do NOT supply) apply via fext on the spindles; the free chassis is
# held up only by the four suspensions, so at q = 0 it sits in vertical
# equilibrium and is marginally free in x/y/yaw -- the honest behavior of a
# vehicle that needs applied forces to hold station.
#
# Springs and shocks (per corner, two TSDAs sharing the LCA mount but not the
# chassis mount, as in quartercar/halfcar): the real HMMWV coil spring is a
# progressive nonlinear curve, linearized to its slope at zero deflection
# (front 3629.923 N / 0.02 m, rear 8020.869 / 0.02); the shock damping
# coefficient is already linear and used directly. Both anchors ride on the
# body that physically carries them -- the chassis for the upper mount, the
# LCA for the lower -- so with the chassis free the spring measures only the
# wishbone's rotation relative to the chassis, never a spurious length change
# from chassis heave/roll (the halfcar lesson). Free lengths are the JSON
# values (front 0.339, rear 0.382). All passive (no 'input').
#
# q layout (nq 48, nv 43): chassis q[0..6] (quat + pos) v[0..5]; rack q[7]
# v[6]; then each corner LCA(1) UCA(1) spindle(quat+pos 7 / spatial 6) post(1).
# Design pose: q = 0 with every quaternion at identity (chassis q[0]=1, each
# spindle's leading quaternion component = 1).

gravity 0 0 -9.81
stab 0.05

body                     # 0: chassis, full HMMWV sprung mass, free-flying
parent -1
joint floating
tree 0 0 0
mass 2086.52
cg 0.056 0 0.239         # HMMWV_Chassis centroid (0.056,0,0.213) lifted +0.026
inertia 1078.52 2955.66 3570.20 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 1: steering rack, slides laterally on the chassis (driver)
parent 0
joint prismatic y
tree 1.43897 0 0.08      # front tierod inboard point, projected to centerline
mass 9.072
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1 1 1 0 0 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- front-left
body                     # 2: FL lower control arm, pivot y=0.307 z=0.026 (exact x axis)
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.68897 0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 3: FL upper control arm, pivot at front/back midpoint
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.53097 0.462 0.2465
mass 5.813
cg 0.052 0.127 -0.0025
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 4: FL spindle assembly (upright+spindle+wheel+tire), at wheel center
parent -1
joint floating
tree 1.64897 0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 -0.0342 0           # upright CG sits 0.159 inboard of the wheel center
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 5: FL shaker post pad at the contact patch -- a driver
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 1.64897 0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# --------------------------------------------------------------- front-right
body                     # 6: FR lower control arm, mirror of body 2
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.68897 -0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 -0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 7: FR upper control arm, mirror of body 3
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree 1.53097 -0.462 0.2465
mass 5.813
cg 0.052 -0.127 -0.0025
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 8: FR spindle assembly, mirror of body 4
parent -1
joint floating
tree 1.64897 -0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 0.0342 0
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 9: FR shaker post pad, mirror of body 5
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree 1.64897 -0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- rear-left
body                     # 10: RL lower control arm, pivot y=0.307 z=0.026 (exact x axis)
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.68897 0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 11: RL upper control arm, pivot at front/back midpoint
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.47596 0.462 0.252
mass 5.813
cg -0.089 0.127 -0.005
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 12: RL spindle assembly, at wheel center
parent -1
joint floating
tree -1.65297 0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 -0.0342 0
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 13: RL shaker post pad, a driver
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree -1.65297 0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rear-right
body                     # 14: RR lower control arm, mirror of body 10
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.68897 -0.307 0.026
mass 23.965
cg 0 -0.240 -0.059
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.8938 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 15: RR upper control arm, mirror of body 11
parent 0
joint revolute x
tree -1.47596 -0.462 0.252
mass 5.813
cg -0.089 -0.127 -0.005
inertia 0.03 0.03 0.06276 0 0 0

body                     # 16: RR spindle assembly, mirror of body 12
parent -1
joint floating
tree -1.65297 -0.91 0
mass 90.555
cg 0 0.0342 0
inertia 4.896 7.581 4.774 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 17: RR shaker post pad, mirror of body 13
parent -1
joint prismatic z
tree -1.65297 -0.91 -0.467
mass 25
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.35 0.35 0.65 0 0 0

# ================================================================ FL loops
loop                     # FL lower ball: LCA_FL outer end to spindle_FL
predecessor 2
successor 4
joint spherical
ptree -0.036 0.48 -0.118
stree 0.004 -0.123 -0.092

loop                     # FL upper ball: UCA_FL outer end to spindle_FL
predecessor 3
successor 4
joint spherical
ptree 0.105 0.254 -0.0055
stree -0.013 -0.194 0.241

loop                     # FL tie rod: RACK to spindle_FL steering arm (STEERED)
predecessor 1
successor 4
joint distance
ptree 0 0.448 0
stree -0.136 -0.089 0.01
length 0.3866588

loop                     # FL driver rod: post_FL pad to wheel center, one tire radius
predecessor 5
successor 4
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ================================================================ FR loops
loop                     # FR lower ball, mirror
predecessor 6
successor 8
joint spherical
ptree -0.036 -0.48 -0.118
stree 0.004 0.123 -0.092

loop                     # FR upper ball, mirror
predecessor 7
successor 8
joint spherical
ptree 0.105 -0.254 -0.0055
stree -0.013 0.194 0.241

loop                     # FR tie rod: RACK to spindle_FR steering arm (STEERED)
predecessor 1
successor 8
joint distance
ptree 0 -0.448 0
stree -0.136 0.089 0.01
length 0.3866588

loop                     # FR driver rod, mirror
predecessor 9
successor 8
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ================================================================ RL loops
loop                     # RL lower ball: LCA_RL outer end to spindle_RL
predecessor 10
successor 12
joint spherical
ptree 0.036 0.48 -0.118
stree 0 -0.123 -0.092

loop                     # RL upper ball: UCA_RL outer end to spindle_RL
predecessor 11
successor 12
joint spherical
ptree -0.177 0.254 -0.01
stree 0 -0.194 0.242

loop                     # RL tie rod: CHASSIS to spindle_RL steering arm (grounded, no steer)
predecessor 0
successor 12
joint distance
ptree -1.46596 0.416 0.085
stree 0.134 -0.089 0.017
length 0.4140749

loop                     # RL driver rod: post_RL pad to wheel center, one tire radius
predecessor 13
successor 12
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ================================================================ RR loops
loop                     # RR lower ball, mirror
predecessor 14
successor 16
joint spherical
ptree 0.036 -0.48 -0.118
stree 0 0.123 -0.092

loop                     # RR upper ball, mirror
predecessor 15
successor 16
joint spherical
ptree -0.177 -0.254 -0.01
stree 0 0.194 0.242

loop                     # RR tie rod: CHASSIS to spindle_RR steering arm (grounded, no steer)
predecessor 0
successor 16
joint distance
ptree -1.46596 -0.416 0.085
stree 0.134 0.089 0.017
length 0.4140749

loop                     # RR driver rod, mirror
predecessor 17
successor 16
joint distance
ptree 0 0 0
stree 0 0 0
length 0.467

# ============================================= spring/shock POIs and TSDAs
# Front chassis anchors on body 0 (chassis); rear too. Arm anchors on each
# LCA. Front spring/shock share the LCA arm point; rear spring and shock have
# slightly different arm points (per the rear JSON).
poi springChassis_FL 0 1.79297 0.51 0.223
poi springArm_FL 2 0.097 0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_FL 0 1.79297 0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_FL 2 0.097 0.236 -0.047

poi springChassis_FR 0 1.79297 -0.51 0.223
poi springArm_FR 6 0.097 -0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_FR 0 1.79297 -0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_FR 6 0.097 -0.236 -0.047

poi springChassis_RL 0 -1.79297 0.502 0.282
poi springArm_RL 10 -0.097 0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_RL 0 -1.79297 0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_RL 10 -0.097 0.237 -0.038

poi springChassis_RR 0 -1.79297 -0.502 0.282
poi springArm_RR 14 -0.097 -0.236 -0.047
poi shockChassis_RR 0 -1.79297 -0.498 0.349
poi shockArm_RR 14 -0.097 -0.237 -0.038

tsda spring_FL              # HMMWV front coil spring, linearized
from springChassis_FL
to springArm_FL
k 181496.15
c 0
l0 0.339

tsda shock_FL              # HMMWV front shock absorber
from shockChassis_FL
to shockArm_FL
k 0
c 19015.5692
l0 0.339

tsda spring_FR
from springChassis_FR
to springArm_FR
k 181496.15
c 0
l0 0.339

tsda shock_FR
from shockChassis_FR
to shockArm_FR
k 0
c 19015.5692
l0 0.339

tsda spring_RL             # HMMWV rear coil spring, linearized
from springChassis_RL
to springArm_RL
k 401043.45
c 0
l0 0.382

tsda shock_RL              # HMMWV rear shock absorber
from shockChassis_RL
to shockArm_RL
k 0
c 36725.2201
l0 0.382

tsda spring_RR
from springChassis_RR
to springArm_RR
k 401043.45
c 0
l0 0.382

tsda shock_RR
from shockChassis_RR
to shockArm_RR
k 0
c 36725.2201
l0 0.382
